  "notes": [
    "[reduce-overhead] host_sequence segments were captured from a SECOND, EAGER instance of lerobot/smolvla_base. Under compile_mode=reduce-overhead this model's whole frame replays as a CUDA graph, so the Python layer body never executes and a layer capture records nothing. The capture is setup rather than measurement -- what is measured is the contention slowdown of replaying a fixed host-launched segment sequence -- but it means this row's segments did NOT come from the compiled frame. pi0.5's compiled frame is not graphed as a unit and captured normally, so its rows are not comparable to this one in that respect.",
    "gpu_idle_ae_total is region time minus the UNION of kernel intervals inside the ae_step NVTX spans, so overlapping kernels are not double-counted. It is the GPU time already free for the next frame's prefix in the ordinary all-GPU run.",
    "T004's E5 may reuse these captures rather than taking new ones; the .nsys-rep files are under raw/ and the exports under nsys/.",
    "Compiled captures run with --no-regions: bench/regions.py's context managers force a graph break under torch.compile (bench/run_e4.py), so a compiled run with regions on would not be the graph the model actually executes. That means no ae_step NVTX spans exist for compiled, and gpu_idle is reported for eager.",
    "Concurrency is measured both ways \u00a713.7 asks for: two CUDA streams in one process and two processes. Whether the high-priority stream argument was accepted is recorded."
  ]
